Chapter: GopSettingsSchema
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Works chapter GopFat16
  cites Works chapter GopSettings

 The refusal arms are the point of this chapter, and they are written so a
 CLAMPING implementation would fail them: each one sets a legal value
 first, then attempts an illegal one, then reads. A clamp answers the
 limit, a refusal answers the value that was already there, and the two
 disagree on every row. A test that only attempted the illegal value from
 the default could not tell the two apart.

 The load row carries the same requirement and its operands are chosen for
 it. The illegal record targets `zone`, whose default is 0 and whose high
 limit is 14, so refusing answers 0, clamping answers 14 and adopting
 answers 99. Targeting `adorn` would have been useless: its high limit IS
 its default, so a clamp and a refusal agree there. `scheme` is the
 positive control on the same row -- a legal record that must land, or an
 implementation refusing everything would score the same as a correct one.

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let keys = [
      gst-int-key 1 "scheme" 0 0 3,
      gst-int-key 2 "adorn" 15 0 15,
      gst-int-key 3 "zone" 0 (0 - 12) 14,
      gst-bool-key 4 "sound" True
    ]
    in let s0 = gst-store keys
    in let l1 = "defaults scheme=" & show (gst-get s0 1 (0 - 1)) & " adorn=" & show (gst-get s0 2 (0 - 1)) & " zone=" & show (gst-get s0 3 (0 - 1)) & " sound=" & show (gst-get-bool s0 4 False) & " count=" & show (s0.st-count)
    in let s1 = gst-or-keep s0 (gst-set s0 1 2)
    in let l2 = "set scheme=" & show (gst-get s1 1 (0 - 1))
    in let r-hi = gst-set s1 1 9
    in let s2 = gst-or-keep s1 r-hi
    in let l3 = "refuse-hi scheme=" & show (gst-get s2 1 (0 - 1)) & " why=" & gst-why r-hi
    in let r-lo = gst-set s2 3 (0 - 20)
    in let s3 = gst-or-keep s2 r-lo
    in let l4 = "refuse-lo zone=" & show (gst-get s3 3 (0 - 1)) & " why=" & gst-why r-lo
    in let s4 = gst-or-keep s3 (gst-set s3 3 (0 - 5))
    in let l5 = "neg zone=" & show (gst-get s4 3 (0 - 1))
    in let r-unk = gst-set s4 99 1
    in let l6 = "unknown why=" & gst-why r-unk
    in let s5 = gst-or-keep s4 (gst-reset s4 1)
    in let s6 = gst-reset-all s5
    in let l7 = "reset scheme=" & show (gst-get s5 1 (0 - 1)) & " all-zone=" & show (gst-get s6 3 (0 - 1))
    in let s7 = gst-or-keep s6 (gst-set-bool s6 4 False)
    in let l8 = "bool sound=" & show (gst-get-bool s7 4 True)
    in let buf = __heap-save
    in let adv = __heap-advance 64
    in let w1 = gfat-put-u32 buf 0 1
    in let w2 = gfat-put-u32 buf 4 (2 + gst-bias)
    in let w3 = gfat-put-u32 buf 8 3
    in let w4 = gfat-put-u32 buf 12 (99 + gst-bias)
    in let w5 = gfat-put-u32 buf 16 99
    in let w6 = gfat-put-u32 buf 20 (1 + gst-bias)
    in let s8 = gst-apply-recs (gst-store keys) buf 0 3 0
    in let l9 = "load scheme=" & show (gst-get s8 1 (0 - 1)) & " zone=" & show (gst-get s8 3 (0 - 1))
    in act
      print-line-uni l1
      print-line-uni l2
      print-line-uni l3
      print-line-uni l4
      print-line-uni l5
      print-line-uni l6
      print-line-uni l7
      print-line-uni l8
      print-line-uni l9
    end

